course: dictionary
lesson: 9448
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Stamp is a good example. «Stamp your feet outside» is an action, where you put your foot down hard and loud. «Stick a stamp on the letter» means a small piece of paper with glue, used for posting.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it talks about letters, posting or ink, stamp means the paper or the tool. If it talks about feet, anger or being cold, stamp means to press your foot down hard.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. Does «put your foot down hard» fit «stamp your feet outside»? Yes, so that is the meaning. Does it fit «a stamp on the letter»? No, so the stamp there is the paper.
fact: Stamp has more than one meaning, so the context decides which one is right.
fact: As a noun, a stamp is a small piece of paper with glue that you stick on a letter to show the postage is paid.
fact: As a noun, a stamp can also be a tool that prints a mark or picture with ink, or the mark it makes.
fact: As a verb, to stamp means to put your foot down hard and loudly, or to press a mark on something.
fact: The noun can be «stamps» for more than one, and the verb can be «stamped» or «stamping».
exercise: «4 stamps on the table and 10 stamps in the box» How many stamps are there altogether? | 6 | *14 | 40 | 10
exercise: «Never hit; walk away, squeeze a pillow, stamp your feet outside or tell an adult instead.» What does stamp mean here? | To glue a small paper on a letter | To hiss and raise your tail | *To put your foot down hard and loudly | To print a picture with ink
exercise: Mia says, «I need a stamp for my letter.» What is a stamp? | A loud cheer at a party | A mark made by a hard kick | To press your foot down hard | *A small paper with glue, to show the postage is paid
test: «At last, right above their heads, they hear cheering, stamping and glasses clinking.» What does stamping mean in this sentence? | Ink marks on paper | Glasses being put away | Small pieces of paper stuck on letters | *Loud feet hitting the floor
test: In Kipling's tale, the Butterfly boasts that if he «stamps his foot», Suleiman's palace will vanish. What does stamps mean here? | To post a letter | To print a mark with ink | To count the stamps in a box | *To put his foot down hard
exam: Which sentence uses stamp as a verb? | *Please stamp your feet to keep warm. | Look at the stamps in the box. | Please put a stamp on the envelope. | The stamp on the card is blue.
